<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Almohad Caliphate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Almohads, Almohad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Almohad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> Muslim empire founded on the religious reform movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a> and established as a state by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-mumin">Abd al-Mu'min</a> in the twelfth century. It overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, promoting a strict doctrine of divine unity. After its defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212 it declined, and it collapsed in the thirteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate.jpg" alt="Almohad Caliphate" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flaspec · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almohad_dynasty_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
